# Railway upload-exclusion list.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND THE MISTAKE THAT CREATED IT
# `railway up` uploads the working directory, and it RESPECTS .gitignore. On
# 2026-09-27 the Standing Interview corpus was made gitignored (so no book text
# can ever enter this public repository) on the assumption that gitignored
# files would still be uploaded. That assumption was wrong -- it was inferred
# from deploy_customer_app.sh's note that `railway up` "does not include the
# .git folder", which says nothing about ignored files. The deploy succeeded,
# the corpus did not ship, and production correctly reported
# {"loaded": false} with the nav entry hidden. Fail-closed worked; the
# mechanism did not.
#
# When this file is present, Railway uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore. That is a
# real hazard: everything .gitignore excludes would start uploading unless it
# is repeated here. So this file is a VERBATIM COPY of .gitignore with exactly
# ONE line removed -- `agent/.si_corpus/` -- and nothing else changed. Every
# other exclusion, including `.env`, is preserved deliberately.
#
# DO NOT hand-edit. Regenerate with `python scripts/sync_railwayignore.py`,
# which re-derives it from .gitignore and is asserted by
# agent/test_standing_interview.py.
#
# ---- begin verbatim copy of .gitignore, minus agent/.si_corpus/ ----
